    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0721" n="463" xml:id="pg463"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1933</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-08T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 8, 1915, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 9, 12.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2562. Department’s 1915, July 6, 7 p. m. In order to have no mistake communicated
                    in writing to Foreign Office that you did not desire to engage in any
                    preliminary negotiations. Think note will come to-morrow. Paragraph 4 (see my
                    2543, July 3, 10 p. m., and 2548, July 5, 7 p. m.) will be changed by offering
                    that a certain number of belligerent passenger ships shall be put under American
                    flag and come under paragraph 2.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
